WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.840
While some former child actors are still working&nbsp;
in front of the camera, others have found their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.280
calling in a variety of careers. From sets&nbsp;
of famous twins to Disney Channel superstars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.920
here's where a number of famous former child&nbsp;
actors ended up and what they're doing today.&nbsp;

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.760
In the early nineties, angelic Mara Wilson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.560
stole hearts across the world. After earning fame&nbsp;
and acclaim for playing the youngest daughter of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:30.960
Sally Field and Robin Williams in Mrs. Doubtfire,&nbsp;
Wilson appeared in the 1994 remake of the classic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:37.280
film Miracle on 34th Street. But you probably&nbsp;
know her best for her leading role in Matilda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:42.720
Roald Dahl's classic story of a sweet,&nbsp;
well-read girl with amazing powers.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:48.080
Sadly, a personal tragedy caused Wilson to stop&nbsp;
acting when she was still young. While the child&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:53.040
star was filming Matilda, her mother passed&nbsp;
away due to complications from breast cancer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.960
leaving her grieving. In the years that&nbsp;
followed, she stepped away from acting.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.320
Wilson ultimately attended New York University,&nbsp;
where she performed a one-woman show about her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:08.640
past, and in 2016, she released a book about&nbsp;
her experiences as a child star. According to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:14.640
Wilson herself, her acting days are over, and&nbsp;
these days, she focuses exclusively on writing.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.560
With his huge eyes, endearing attitude,&nbsp;
and clear comedic chops, Macaulay Culkin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:27.280
was catapulted to stardom in the 1990 film Home&nbsp;
Alone. Culkin portrayed young Kevin McCallister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.200
left behind when his parents go on&nbsp;
a holiday trip. Though Culkin had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.720
already appeared in Uncle Buck in 1989,&nbsp;
Home Alone was an even bigger success,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:41.680
spawning sequels and making Culkin one of&nbsp;
the most famous young actors of his era.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:47.360
After appearing in the nineties films Home Alone&nbsp;
2: Lost in New York, Richie Rich, and My Girl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.960
among other films, Culkin took a break from acting&nbsp;
to attend school. Before long, he returned to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:58.640
limelight, ready to change his image all together&nbsp;
with daring, edgy films like Party Monster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:03.600
and Saved! Despite the fact that Culkin's roles&nbsp;
have been relatively small throughout the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:09.040
he's stayed in the public eye, from high-profile&nbsp;
advertisements mocking his Home Alone success&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:14.640
to his odd Velvet Underground cover band. In&nbsp;
2020, Culkin teamed up with Ryan Murphy to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.760
appear in future installments of the creator's&nbsp;
anthology series, American Horror Story.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:26.480
After his big brother Macaulay won over audiences,&nbsp;
it was time for Kieran Culkin - who appeared in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.040
small roles in both Home Alone movies -&nbsp;
to take center stage. Like his brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.760
the younger Culkin also began his career as&nbsp;
a child actor, working with Steve Martin and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:41.440
Diane Keaton as the adorable Matty in Father&nbsp;
of the Bride and Father of the Bride: Part 2.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:46.960
More recently, Culkin reprised his role&nbsp;
as Matty in a COVID-19-inspired third film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:52.320
in the Father of the Bride franchise, where&nbsp;
he appeared with the original cast. By 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:58.240
Culkin was plenty famous in his own right and&nbsp;
scored an Emmy nom for his role as the outlandish,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:03.200
boorish Roman Roy on HBO's hit&nbsp;
drama Succession. Kieran may be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.280
the younger Culkin, but he's certainly&nbsp;
achieved plenty of success on his own.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:14.240
Amandla Stenberg may have made her film debut&nbsp;
in 2011 at just 13 years old in the action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:19.600
flick Colombiana, but most audiences will&nbsp;
recognize Stenberg from her breakout role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:24.160
in The Hunger Games in 2012. Adapted&nbsp;
from Suzanne Collins's book trilogy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:29.680
The Hunger Games imagined a dystopian world where&nbsp;
impoverished families must send their children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:36.000
into a horrifying fight to the death each year.&nbsp;
Stenberg plays the tiny yet incredibly smart Rue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.880
who ends up teaming up with Jennifer&nbsp;
Lawrence's protagonist, Katniss Everdeen.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.840
In the years since The Hunger Games, Stenberg&nbsp;
has continued acting. Perhaps most notably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.720
Stenberg led a high-profile and acclaimed&nbsp;
adaptation of the young adult novel The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:57.360
Hate U Give in 2018 as Starr Carter, who&nbsp;
witnesses a police officer kill an unarmed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:02.320
young Black man. Stenberg has also appeared&nbsp;
in television projects like Sleepy Hollow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.280
Everything, Everything, and 2020's Mr. Eddy.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.240
One of the most famous child stars&nbsp;
of all time, Neil Patrick Harris,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:17.360
earned fame and acclaim as the title character in&nbsp;
Doogie Howser, M.D., which began its run in 1989&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:22.960
with Harris as a genius boy doctor. Harris could&nbsp;
have easily retired after the success of the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:29.200
but instead, he kept working and became one of the&nbsp;
most popular television actors of his generation.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:33.040
After lampooning himself in Harold&nbsp;
and Kumar Go to White Castle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:39.360
Harris took on his next big television role. In&nbsp;
2005, Harris joined the cast of the CBS sitcom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:44.720
How I Met Your Mother as the womanizer with a&nbsp;
heart of gold, Barney Stinson. He's also appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:50.880
in shows like Netflix's A Series of Unfortunate&nbsp;
Events. From dramatic turns in Gone Girl to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:56.400
Tony Award-winning run on Broadway in Hedwig&nbsp;
and the Angry Inch, Harris has remained one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:02.000
Hollywood's most beloved and recognizable faces&nbsp;
for years. Doogie may have been an iconic role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:07.600
but clearly, Harris raised the bar to create even&nbsp;
more memorable performances throughout the years.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:14.080
Nickelodeon spawned plenty of young stars during&nbsp;
its heyday, thanks to ensemble comedies like All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:19.520
That and The Amanda Show. Though a fair amount&nbsp;
of familiar faces popped up on The Amanda Show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:24.720
it also helped launch some careers within the&nbsp;
network-and when it came to a young Josh Peck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:28.720
the series served as a launching&nbsp;
pad for his next big project.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:34.400
After The Amanda Show, Josh Peck went on to&nbsp;
headline Drake &amp; Josh, a Nickelodeon sitcom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.040
alongside Drake Bell. Since then, Peck&nbsp;
has continued acting. In recent years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:44.640
he's appeared with John Stamos in shows like&nbsp;
Grandfathered and in Fox's short-lived Pitch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:51.040
Currently, Peck runs his own podcast, "Curious&nbsp;
with Josh Peck." In an LTV interview, Josh said,

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:54.480
"Going straight to my audience is really&nbsp;
powerful because I don't have to wait for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:59.280
anyone to give me permission or hope&nbsp;
that something is received correctly."

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:04.160
He's also slated to appear in Disney+'s&nbsp;
upcoming Turner &amp; Hooch reboot.

00:06:05.051 --> 00:06:10.800
For a certain generation of young girls, their&nbsp;
childhoods were defined by the famous twins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:16.800
Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen, who rose to prominence&nbsp;
as Michelle Tanner on Full House. After the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:21.920
overwhelming success of the show, which cast both&nbsp;
twins as Michelle at just six months old, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:26.320
Olsens continued their winning streak, appearing&nbsp;
in their own movies by the time they were six&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:31.760
years old. Between theatrical releases like It&nbsp;
Takes Two and New York Minute to direct-to-video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:38.400
films like Passport to Paris, the Olsen twins&nbsp;
were everywhere for most of the 1990s and 2000s.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:42.480
However, when the twins turned eighteen&nbsp;
and officially left acting behind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:46.880
they've remained relevant throughout the years,&nbsp;
thanks to their work in the fashion industry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:50.880
Together, the Olsen twins have created&nbsp;
high-end fashion lines that include&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:55.680
Elizabeth &amp; James and The Row, both of&nbsp;
which have proven enormously successful.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:02.640
If you watch the 1994 Best Picture Forrest Gump&nbsp;
closely, you might notice a young Haley Joel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:09.760
Osment as Forrest's son. Just a few years later,&nbsp;
Osment scored a huge role in M. Night Shyamalan's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:15.920
film The Sixth Sense. As Cole Sear, Osment&nbsp;
perfectly portrayed a young boy who can see ghosts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:21.200
that don't know they've died. He even earned an&nbsp;
Oscar nomination for his performance. In the years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:27.360
that followed, Osment continued his acting streak&nbsp;
with films like Pay It Forward and A.I. Artificial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:32.560
Intelligence, as well as voice appearances&nbsp;
in movies like The Hunchback of Notre Dame.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:36.400
Osment's career has never returned to&nbsp;
the heights he did with The Sixth Sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:41.520
but in recent years, the talented actor has&nbsp;
shown up in small appearances on popular shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:48.000
like HBO's Silicon Valley, Amazon's The&nbsp;
Boys, and FX's What We Do in the Shadows.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:53.280
In 2001, Disney Channel viewers&nbsp;
found their new favorite series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:58.240
Lizzie McGuire, which told the story of an&nbsp;
average, lovable middle schooler named Lizzie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:02.480
who was trying to get through the seventh&nbsp;
grade. Duff won over audiences everywhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:07.760
with her hilarious yet heartfelt performance as&nbsp;
Lizzie. Ultimately, the show proved so successful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:13.520
that it even spawned its own feature film,&nbsp;
The Lizzie McGuire Movie, released in 2003.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:17.200
Through the years, she's worked&nbsp;
as both a musician and an actress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:22.400
After the success of Lizzie McGuire, Duff&nbsp;
appeared in teen fare like Agent Cody Banks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:26.080
A Cinderella Story, and both&nbsp;
Cheaper by the Dozen remakes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:32.640
She also recorded huge albums like Metamorphosis&nbsp;
in 2003. Duff returned to television as an adult,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:38.400
starring in Darren Star's delightful comedy&nbsp;
Younger as publishing executive Kelsey Peters.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:44.480
If you're an Adam Sandler fan, you probably&nbsp;
remember his silly yet emotional comedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:50.000
Big Daddy-and if you do, you definitely&nbsp;
remember his adorable adopted on-screen son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:55.440
Julian. This role was the big screen debut&nbsp;
for young twins Dylan and Cole Sprouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:59.760
who would go on to work with Sandler&nbsp;
again in movies like Eight Crazy Nights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:05.200
and occasionally take on their own roles. In&nbsp;
2005, the dynamic duo got their own series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:10.320
The Suite Life of Zack and Cody on the&nbsp;
Disney Channel, in which they played twins.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.400
After a spin-off and a television movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:17.360
the Sprouse twins left their acting careers&nbsp;
behind temporarily to attend college. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:23.840
Sprouses attended New York University from 2011&nbsp;
to 2015. After that, Cole ultimately returned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:30.720
to television as Jughead Jones on the CW's&nbsp;
Riverdale in 2018, while Dylan runs All-Wise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:36.640
Meadery in Brooklyn and in 2020 snagged a&nbsp;
major role in the movie After We Collided.

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:44.320
When it comes to childhood tearjerkers, few&nbsp;
films loom quite as large as 1991's My Girl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:49.920
the story of the close friendship between young&nbsp;
Vada -played by Anna Chlumsky - and Thomas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:55.520
portrayed by Macaulay Culkin. My Girl has one&nbsp;
of the most tragic endings in cinematic history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:59.920
thanks in large part to the emotional&nbsp;
performances by Chlumsky and Culkin.

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:04.800
After appearing in My Girl 2, Chlumsky took&nbsp;
a significant break from acting and attended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:10.240
the University of Chicago, earning a degree&nbsp;
in international studies in 2002. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:15.280
Chlumsky still wanted to act, and after training&nbsp;
at New York City's Atlantic Acting School,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:21.920
she booked the role of a lifetime as Amy&nbsp;
Brookheimer on HBO's biting political satire Veep.

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:26.400
Alongside Julia Louis-Dreyfus and&nbsp;
a host of other talented comedians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:31.760
Chlumsky shined as the uptight, eternally&nbsp;
stressed Amy, and earned six Emmy nods for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:35.760
her supporting role. If you were a fan&nbsp;
of My Girl and haven't caught Veep yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:39.760
it might be shocking to see little&nbsp;
Vada display such a foul mouth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:44.720
but there's no denying that Chlumsky's&nbsp;
performance on Veep is a comedic tour de force.

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:52.000
When it comes to instantly recognizable child&nbsp;
stars, few faces are as familiar as Jonathan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:58.960
Lipnicki, who cornered the market on portrayals&nbsp;
of precocious children in the 1990s and 2000s.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:04.800
In 1996, Lipnicki earned instant fame and&nbsp;
acclaim alongside Tom Cruise and Renée&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:10.240
Zellweger in the smash hit Jerry Maguire. From&nbsp;
there, he went on to movies like Dr. Dolittle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:16.960
Stuart Little and its 2002 sequel, as well&nbsp;
as The Little Vampire, and 2002's Like Mike.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:20.880
In the years since his childhood success,&nbsp;
Lipnicki has appeared in a string of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:26.080
independent films like For the Love of&nbsp;
Money, Limelight, and 2018's Andover.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:30.320
"There's nothing I'd rather do with my life.&nbsp;
You know, whether I'm doing big movies like I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:33.520
did in my childhood, or you know, I've&nbsp;
actually done more work as an adult."

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:38.160
He's also appeared on a few television&nbsp;
programs, including competition and reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:43.920
shows like Drop the Mic, a celebrity edition of&nbsp;
Worst Cooks in America, and Celebs Go Dating.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:50.240
Before her breakout role, Dakota Fanning appeared&nbsp;
in small roles in commercials and on shows like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:56.800
E.R., but it was her starring role in the 2001&nbsp;
drama I Am Sam alongside Sean Penn that really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.800 --> 00:12:02.560
put Fanning on the map. From there, Fanning became&nbsp;
one of the most in-demand young actresses around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:06.880
appearing in everything from romantic&nbsp;
comedies like Uptown Girls to sci-fi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:12.000
blockbusters like War of the Worlds to&nbsp;
fantasy fare like the Twilight Saga.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:17.360
Fanning hasn't stopped working for a second.&nbsp;
Her recent high-profile roles include a cameo in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:23.360
2018's Ocean's 8, a scene-stealing turn in Once&nbsp;
Upon a Time in… Hollywood, and a leading role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:29.760
on the television series The Alienist. Clearly,&nbsp;
Fanning navigated her years as a child star well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:33.920
and moviegoers should expect many more&nbsp;
great performances from her to come.

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:37.280
Check out one of our newest&nbsp;
videos right here! Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:40.880
even more Looper videos about your&nbsp;
favorite stuff are coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:46.693
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit&nbsp;
the bell so you don't miss a single one.

